  "rules": [
    "When recent history shows a strong upward trend followed by a flat or slightly declining sentiment score (e.g., Example 1), the model significantly underestimates the upside potential and fails to capture volatility spikes.",
    "In low-sentiment environments with high historical volatility (Examples 2-5), the model exhibits a severe downward bias, predicting a steady decline while the true outcome frequently reverses direction or recovers sharply.",
    "The model consistently ignores mean reversion signals; it extrapolates linear trends from recent data rather than accounting for the tendency of carbon prices to oscillate around historical averages after extreme moves.",
    "When sentiment history contains isolated spikes (e.g., 0.40) amidst otherwise neutral readings, the model fails to weight these as catalysts for immediate price acceleration or reversal.",
    "The forecast horizon is systematically biased toward the most recent trend direction; if the last 5 days are flat, the model assumes continuation rather than anticipating a breakout driven by latent sentiment shifts."
  ]
}
